      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9223321080207825,
      "reading_order": 2,
      "text": "11. 1 kg saturated solution contains 200 g of solute.\n$\\therefore (1000 - 200) \\text{ g} = 800 \\text{ g}$ solvent dissolves 200 g\nof solute.\n$\\therefore 100 \\text{ g}$ solvent dissolves $\\frac{200 \\times 100}{800} \\text{ g}$.\n$= 25 \\text{ g}$ of solute\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_3e28735a-29a8-40c8-bd7f-dccfdb8be365_10_block_002",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 213.0,
        "y1": 727.0,
        "x2": 1171.0,
        "y2": 1326.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.925289511680603,
      "reading_order": 3,
      "text": "12. 100 g of solution has 10 g of solute.\n$\\therefore$ 1 kg of the solution has 100 g of solute.\n$\\therefore (1000 - 100) \\text{ g} = 900 \\text{ g}$ solvent has 100 g of\nsolute dissolved in it. The solubility of the sol-\nute is 25.\n$\\therefore 900 \\text{ g}$ of solvent can dissolve $\\left( \\frac{25}{100} \\times 900 \\right)\\text{g} =$\n225 g of solute.\n$\\therefore (225 - 100) \\text{ g} = 125 \\text{ g}$ of solute has to be added\nto saturate the solution.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_3e28735a-29a8-40c8-bd7f-dccfdb8be365_10_block_003",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 215.0,
        "y1": 1352.0,
        "x2": 1131.0,
        "y2": 1605.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9003024697303772,
      "reading_order": 4,
      "text": "13. Electrochemical equivalent = $x$\n$\\therefore$ Mass of the metal obtained at the cathode\n$= x \\times 96,500 \\times 0.5 = 48,250 \\, x \\, \\mathrm{g}$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_3e28735a-29a8-40c8-bd7f-dccfdb8be365_10_block_004",
