      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8541155457496643,
      "reading_order": 5,
      "text": "14. $1 \\mathrm{amp} \\times 1 \\mathrm{s} = 1$ Coulomb\n1 Coulomb charge deposits $m$ g of metal.\n$P$ Coulombs charge deposits $(P \\times m)$ g of metal.\nAtomic wt. of the metal is $n$.\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{Valency} = \\frac{\\text{atomic weight}}{\\text{equivalent weight}} = \\frac{n}{m \\times p}$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
